NAME
        nodetool satellite_admin - Manage satellite datacenter failover

SYNOPSIS
        nodetool [(-h <host> | --host <host>)] [(-p <port> | --port <port>)]
                [(-pw <password> | --password <password>)]
                [(-pwf <passwordFilePath> | --password-file <passwordFilePath>)]
                [(-u <username> | --username <username>)] satellite_admin <command>
                [<args>]

        nodetool [(-h <host> | --host <host>)] [(-p <port> | --port <port>)]
                [(-pw <password> | --password <password>)]
                [(-pwf <passwordFilePath> | --password-file <passwordFilePath>)]
                [(-u <username> | --username <username>)] satellite_admin status [--]
                <keyspace>

        nodetool [(-h <host> | --host <host>)] [(-p <port> | --port <port>)]
                [(-pw <password> | --password <password>)]
                [(-pwf <passwordFilePath> | --password-file <passwordFilePath>)]
                [(-u <username> | --username <username>)] satellite_admin advance
                [--ack] [--barrier] [--force] [(-r <rangesStr> | --ranges <rangesStr>)]
                [--] <keyspace>

OPTIONS
        -h <host>, --host <host>
            Node hostname or ip address

        -p <port>, --port <port>
            Remote jmx agent port number

        -pw <password>, --password <password>
            Remote jmx agent password

        -pwf <passwordFilePath>, --password-file <passwordFilePath>
            Path to the JMX password file

        -u <username>, --username <username>
            Remote jmx agent username

COMMANDS
        With no arguments, Display help information

        status
            Show satellite failover status for a keyspace
        advance
            Advance satellite failover for a keyspace

            With --ranges option, Token ranges to process (format: start:end,start:
            end). Defaults to local ranges if not specified.

            With --ack option, Only advance through epoch ack and paxos repair
            (TRANSITION_ACK -> TRANSITION)

            With --barrier option, Only process MT barrier for TRANSITION ranges
            (TRANSITION -> NORMAL)

            With --force option, Skip gate evaluation and commit state transitions
            directly
